<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lisbon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lisbon is the capital of Portugal, on the estuary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a>. It was the centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>, from which fleets sailed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> and where imperial trade was concentrated. The Portuguese court left Lisbon for Brazil in 1807 to escape <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s invasion, a move that led eventually to the founding of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lisbon.jpg" alt="Lisbon" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Vitor Oliveira from Torres Vedras, PORTUGAL · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lisboa_-_Portugal_(52597836992).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
